WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.360
I love this country, Oprah.

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:02.720
I'm not trying to avoid
my taxes.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.400
I was gonna pay my taxes,
Oprah.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:05.920
I know you was.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.240
-I was, I was.
-I know you was.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.240
But then the album flopped.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:10.800
Aha.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.960
So the album flopped,
so we actually didn't--

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.320
-we didn't have--
-I don't even think--

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.800
you know, the way it's written,
I don't even think--

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:19.600
it doesn't even sound like

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.880
you were trying to
avoid your taxes.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.160
You were just like--
you don't even know

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.200
you're supposed to be
payin' your taxes.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.600
Yeah, I wasn't paying attention
to that kinda stuff.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.080
Well, I-I know you're up with
your taxes now, Will.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.000
We know that for sure,
okay?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.160
So right before Fresh Prince
of Bel-Air, I think--

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.600
people would be
surprised to know;

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.280
this is the first time
I realized this--

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.040
is that you basically
lost everything.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.800
The government
seized your cars.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.440
It took your home.
You ended up in jail.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.840
And you describe it
in two words, actually:

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.600
-rock bottom.
-Rock bottom.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.240
What was at the root
of that downfall, Will?

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.440
You know what?
It's like...

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.280
And the life lesson
you took from it.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.920
So w-what--you know...

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.760
-When it rains, it pours.
-Yeah.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.840
Right? So, um, you know,
getting into the fight

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.200
at the radio station,

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.440
you know,
Charlie punching the dude

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.000
-that landed me in jail.
-In jail.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.960
So the money is gone,
the car's gone.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.640
I'm layin' on the floor

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.920
in a jail cell, and I'm like...

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.720
you've got to be kidding me.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.960
I won a Grammy
eight months ago, right?

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.120
Like...what is happening?

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.920
-Mm-hmm.
-And...it's just that--

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.080
just that--the spiral,
when it--

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.520
when it starts goin'
the other way,

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.880
it's like sometimes you just
have to get out the way

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.360
and just wait till the--
the, you know,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.920
-the downward spiral stops.
-But it's a spiral

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.080
that you make so very clear
in Will that you created.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.520
-Yes.
-And now you can see it

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.640
yourself, you see how...

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.560
the energy of yourself,
everything that you were doing

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.720
created that exact moment.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.240
Yeah, I talk about the, um,

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.320
the idea of natural destruction

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.240
-versus self-destruction.
-Yeah.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.240
And, you know,

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:11.600
907
01:37:29,427 --&gt; 01:37:33,264&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.880
impermanence is the law
of the universe.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.720
So things are going to
deteriorate.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.120
Everything's gonna grow.
It's gonna deteriorate and die,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.720
and you gotta be ready
to make the next thing,

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.560
and that's natural, right?

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.720
So we all have to contend
with the entropy of the...

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.520
-Correct.
-The universe in that way.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.640
That's why it's such a crime
when you do it to yourself.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.800
-It's like...
-And that's when you

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.760
-hate yourself the most.
-Don't do it to yourself!

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.800
I love when you say this,
though.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.800
"There's a strange thing
that happens

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.320
when somebody falls:

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.040
your demise somehow
proves to everybody

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.040
you've ever disagreed with
that they were right

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:48.800
and you were wrong.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.000
They develop a smugness
and seem to get a brutal enjoyment

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.200
out of the fact that God
is finally punishing you.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.520
People tend to have
a schizophrenic relationship

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.760
with winners--
if you're down too long,

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.360
you become an underdog

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.960
and they feel impelled
to root for you.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.640
But if you're ever unfortunate
enough to be up too long,

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.600
you better get a helmet."

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:07.840
Helmet.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.280
Amen to that!

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.600
-Don't we know that?
-Yes. Absolutely.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.160
That's one of the things
that I hope people

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.560
can take away from the book
when you see the...

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.560
That's--that's right.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.520
You know, like that's--

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.160
you're not gonna
get around that.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.880
-Yep.
-You're not gonna get around

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.480
the rise and fall
and the rise and fall of--

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.520
You just gotta be able
to hold on to yourself.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.200
You just gotta be able to
hold on, and it's like it's...

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.040
endure when it's time
to endure,

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.080
enjoy when it's time to enjoy,
you know?

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:48.880
But you're not gonna get around
the ups and downs of that.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.400
And, you know, took me
a few of 'em to realize

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.120
that, um, it's not because
I'm stupid.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.240
It's not because I'm weak.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.960
-It's not because I'm a coward.
-Coward.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.160
It's not any of that.
It's like

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.880
that's what life is.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:07.600
Yeah.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.200
-Yeah.
-That's what it is!

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.080
You know,
and all of those things

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.320
are the natural ebb and flow
and the natural rise and fall,

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:17.200
and...

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.160
if we can relax, you know,

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.160
-and settle into it...
-Yeah.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.200
Then we can enjoy, you know,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.280
when the springtime is there,

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.840
and we just buckle down
when the winter comes.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:41.840
But we're not gonna be able
to get around seasons.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:50.488
And also, your father had

00:04:50.488 --> 00:04:51.340
the exact same definition.

00:04:51.339 --> 00:04:52.387
I was saying,
"I thought that was

00:04:52.387 --> 00:04:53.304
my own personal definition."

00:04:53.304 --> 00:04:54.352
But then I read it
and I thought,

00:04:54.352 --> 00:04:55.629
"Guess I'm not the only one
who had it."

00:04:55.629 --> 00:04:57.627
Your father has the exact same
definition of luck that I have:

00:04:57.627 --> 00:04:59.003
that luck is preparation
meeting the moment

00:04:59.003 --> 00:05:00.161
-of opportunity.
-Opportunity.

